# Valgrind suppressions for ODBC DRIVER-INTERNAL defects.
#
# The valgrind tier in run_odbc.sh asserts that WE make no invalid access. A
# driver manager dlopens third-party libraries, and what those do inside
# themselves is not gBASIC's to fix or to fail on.
#
# Each entry below was ISOLATED before being suppressed -- reproduced by a
# plain C program that calls the ODBC API directly with string literals, with
# no gBASIC code in the stack at all. A suppression added without that step
# would be indistinguishable from hiding our own bug.
#
# The suppressions are NARROW on purpose: they name the specific driver object
# and entry point. A blanket "anything inside a driver .so" rule would also
# hide uninitialised data that WE passed in, which is precisely the defect
# class this tier exists to catch.

# MariaDB Connector/ODBC 3.2.6 (libmaodbc.so) reads an uninitialised value in
# its own SQLPrepare path. Reproduced standalone with:
#   SQLPrepare(stmt, (SQLCHAR *)"select 1", SQL_NTS)
# on a literal, in C, outside gBASIC entirely.
{
   mariadb-odbc-sqlprepare-uninitialised
   Memcheck:Cond
   obj:*/odbc/libmaodbc.so
   fun:SQLPrepare
   fun:SQLPrepare
   ...
}
